# ============================================================================
# DEVELOPMENT DEPENDENCIES (loose pins)
# ============================================================================
# Everything from requirements.in PLUS the tools needed to develop, test,
# lint, type-check, security-check, and ship the project.  Runtime packages
# are pulled in automatically via the -r line below.
#
# THIS FILE IS A SCAFFOLD TEMPLATE.
# It was copied from _copilot-shared\scaffold\requirements-dev.in.
# Edit this file when adding or removing a dev-only dependency, then
# regenerate the locked file:
#
#   pip-compile requirements-dev.in
#
# That command creates requirements-dev.txt with exact version pins.
# Commit requirements-dev.txt.
# ============================================================================

-r requirements.in

# --- Testing -----------------------------------------------------------------
pytest                          # Test framework for unit and integration tests
pytest-cov                      # Coverage reporting plugin for pytest
pytest-mock                     # Thin mocker fixture wrapping unittest.mock
pytest-xdist                    # Parallel test execution (-n auto in sanity.bat)

# --- Linting / formatting / typing ------------------------------------------
ruff                            # Fast Python linter and formatter (replaces flake8/black)
mypy                            # Static type checker for type-hint correctness

# --- Security scanning -------------------------------------------------------
bandit                          # Find common security issues in Python code
detect-secrets                  # Prevent secrets from being committed

# --- Build / dependency management -------------------------------------------
pip-tools                       # Provides pip-compile for deterministic dependency locks
pre-commit                      # Git-hook automation (.pre-commit-config.yaml)

# ============================================================================
# COMMON ADDITIONS — uncomment what you need
# ============================================================================

# --- Type stubs (add stubs for any typed third-party libraries you use) ------
# pandas-stubs                  # Official type stubs for pandas (PEP 561)
# types-requests                # Type stubs for the requests library

# --- HTTP mocking for tests --------------------------------------------------
# responses                     # Mock HTTP responses in unit tests (requests-based)
# pytest-httpserver             # Spin up a local HTTP server inside tests

# --- NOT always on internal mirrors — install separately if needed -----------
# pip-audit                     # Audit installed packages for known CVEs

# --- pip version pin (uncomment if pip-tools is incompatible with latest pip) -
# pip<25                        # pip-tools 7.4.x is incompatible with pip 25+
